Date: Sun, 27 Aug 2000 21:06:14 +0000
To: freebsd-alpha
Subject: Re: hd-only install
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=freebsd-alpha&m=103030594008557


Ada Lim writes:
 > How do I install FreeBSD on a machine that only has a hard disk and no
 > other removable media?  NetBSD can install through bootp/tftp...

The easiest way is to netboot via bootp/tftp.

You'll want to extract the kernel from
ftp://ftp.freebsd.org/pub/FreeBSD/releases/alpha/4.1-RELEASE/floppies/boot.flp 

Then setup a diskless root area that looks like this:

<8:50am>blah/gallatin:~>ls /j/diskless/
boot/           kernel.gz*      mfsroot.gz
<8:51am>blah/gallatin:~>ls /j/diskless/boot/
netboot*

You want to use "/j/diskless/boot/netboot" as your boot file.
It will then load the kernel.

You can copy netboot from another FreeBSD/alpha box or just fetch it
from http://www.cs.duke.edu/~gallatin/netboot.gz

Drew

