Hi there,

Attached a log file of a successful FreeBSD boot on a Tincup.
This was done using a pre-installed FreeBSD SCSI disk moved
over from a AS2100. (I know, it is 4.1-RC but that was the
only disk I could lay my hands upon on short notice).

I'll make it run a buildworld to see if it runs stable. In short
summary it appears the AS4100 'does not want to boot install media
floppy or CD' phenomenon is portable to AS1200. Which is not too much
of a surprise.

cheers,
Wilko
